# Numbers outside the forms of the JSON schema

```catala
declaration scope S:
  input i content integer
  input d content decimal
  input m content money
  output ri content integer

scope S:
  definition ri equals i
```

An integer is a number without fraction or exponent:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":1e3,"d":1,"m":1} --disable-warnings
┌─[RESULT]─ S ─
│ ri = 1,000
└─
```

or a string of decimal digits:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":"0x1F","d":1,"m":1} --disable-warnings
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Failed to validate JSON:
│    At /i, unexpected string "0x1F" instead of an integer (integral number or string of digits)
│  
│  Expected JSON object of the form:
│    { "i": $integer,
│      "d": $decimal,
│      "m": $money }
│    $decimal:
│      /* Catala Decimal */
│      number
│      || integer
│      || /^-?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(/.[0-9]+)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?$|^-?[0-9]+/[0-9]*[1-9][0-9]*$/
│    $integer:
│      /* Catala Integer */
│      integer || /^-?[0-9]+$/
│    $money:
│      /* Catala Money */
│      integer
│      || number
│      || /^-?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(/.[0-9]+)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?$/
│
└─
#return code 123#
```

A fraction needs a non-zero denominator:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":1,"d":"1/0","m":1} --disable-warnings
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Failed to validate JSON:
│    At /d, unexpected string "1/0" instead of a decimal (number, numeric string or fraction)
│  
│  Expected JSON object of the form:
│    { "i": $integer,
│      "d": $decimal,
│      "m": $money }
│    $decimal:
│      /* Catala Decimal */
│      number
│      || integer
│      || /^-?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(/.[0-9]+)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?$|^-?[0-9]+/[0-9]*[1-9][0-9]*$/
│    $integer:
│      /* Catala Integer */
│      integer || /^-?[0-9]+$/
│    $money:
│      /* Catala Money */
│      integer
│      || number
│      || /^-?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(/.[0-9]+)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?$/
│
└─
#return code 123#
```

Money is not given as a fraction:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":1,"d":1,"m":"1/3"} --disable-warnings
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Failed to validate JSON:
│    At /m, unexpected string "1/3" instead of an amount (number or numeric string)
│  
│  Expected JSON object of the form:
│    { "i": $integer,
│      "d": $decimal,
│      "m": $money }
│    $decimal:
│      /* Catala Decimal */
│      number
│      || integer
│      || /^-?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(/.[0-9]+)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?$|^-?[0-9]+/[0-9]*[1-9][0-9]*$/
│    $integer:
│      /* Catala Integer */
│      integer || /^-?[0-9]+$/
│    $money:
│      /* Catala Money */
│      integer
│      || number
│      || /^-?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(/.[0-9]+)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?$/
│
└─
#return code 123#
```

Strict JSON: no comments, no NaN:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":1/*c*/,"d":1,"m":1} --disable-warnings
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Failed to parse JSON:
│    expected ',' or '}' at byte 6
│
└─
#return code 123#
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":1,"d":NaN,"m":1} --disable-warnings
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  Failed to parse JSON:
│    unexpected character at byte 11
│
└─
#return code 123#
```

Neither a file nor JSON:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input no_such_file.json --disable-warnings
Usage: [01mcatala interpret[m [[01m--help[m] [[04mOPTION[m]… [04mFILE[m
catala: option [01m--input[m: argument is neither a file nor a valid JSON value.
#return code 124#
```
